<div class="min-h-screen bg-surface text-on-surface">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mb-12">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-label font-black tracking-widest uppercase text-on-surface/50 hover:text-primary transition-colors mb-8"
      >
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-base">arrow_back</span> Chitline
      </a>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black text-on-surface mt-4 mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-on-surface/50 font-label">
        Effective May 1, 2025 &middot; Last updated May 1, 2025
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none space-y-10 font-body text-on-surface/80 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          1. Acceptance of Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or using Chitline ("Service", "we", "us"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          By creating an account, you represent that you are at least 18 years of age and are authorized to bind the business or organization you are registering on behalf of. These terms constitute a legal agreement between you and Chitline, a company based in British Columbia, Canada.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          2. Service Description
        </h2>
        <p>
          Chitline provides a subscription-based software platform for independent food service operators, including:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>The Rail</strong> — Kitchen display and order queue management</li>
          <li><strong>The Studio</strong> — Menu editing and item management</li>
          <li><strong>The Counter</strong> — Customer-facing online ordering interface</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Chitline charges a flat monthly subscription fee with no per-order commissions. We do not take a cut of your sales.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          3. Accounts and Security
        </h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activity that occurs under your account. You agree to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>Provide accurate and complete information when registering</li>
          <li>
            Promptly notify us at
            <a href="mailto:support@chitline.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">
              support@chitline.com
            </a>
            of any unauthorized use or suspected security breach
          </li>
          <li>Not share your login credentials with unauthorized parties</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We are not liable for losses resulting from unauthorized use of your account that occurred through no fault of ours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          4. Subscriptions and Payment
        </h2>

        <h3 class="font-label font-black tracking-wide uppercase text-sm text-on-surface/60 mt-4 mb-2">
          Plans and Pricing
        </h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Starter:</strong> $79/month CAD — single location</li>
          <li><strong>Pro:</strong> $149/month CAD — multiple locations and advanced features</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">
          All prices are in Canadian dollars and are exclusive of applicable taxes. Chitline may offer additional paid add-ons (e.g., menu setup services) at separately disclosed prices.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-label font-black tracking-wide uppercase text-sm text-on-surface/60 mt-4 mb-2">
          Free Trial
        </h3>
        <p>
          New accounts receive a 14-day free trial. A valid payment method is required at signup. If you do not cancel before the trial ends, your subscription will automatically begin and your card will be charged.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-label font-black tracking-wide uppercase text-sm text-on-surface/60 mt-4 mb-2">
          Billing and Cancellation
        </h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>
            Subscriptions are billed monthly in advance on the anniversary of your plan start date
          </li>
          <li>
            You may cancel at any time from your billing settings; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period
          </li>
          <li>We do not provide prorated refunds for partial months</li>
          <li>
            If a payment fails, we will attempt to retry; service may be suspended after a reasonable grace period if payment cannot be collected
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-label font-black tracking-wide uppercase text-sm text-on-surface/60 mt-4 mb-2">
          Price Changes
        </h3>
        <p>
          We may change our subscription pricing with at least 30 days' written notice to the email address on your account. Continued use of the Service after the effective date of a price change constitutes acceptance of the new price.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">5. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to use Chitline only for lawful food service and restaurant operations. You must not:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li>
            Reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to extract the source code of the Service
          </li>
          <li>Resell or sublicense access to the Service without written permission</li>
          <li>Use the Service to transmit spam, malware, or unlawful content</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any system or data</li>
          <li>Use automated bots or scrapers against the Service</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You are solely responsible for the accuracy of your menu, pricing, product descriptions, and order fulfillment. Chitline does not verify the accuracy of operator-provided content.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You are responsible for ensuring your use of the Service complies with all applicable local, provincial, and federal laws, including food service licensing, consumer protection, and tax collection obligations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">6. Customer Data</h2>
        <p>
          When customers place orders through your Chitline ordering page, you are the data controller for their personal information (name, contact details, order history). Chitline processes this data as a service provider on your behalf.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You are responsible for having an appropriate privacy policy for your customers and for complying with applicable privacy laws regarding the collection and use of their data. You must not use customer data collected through Chitline for purposes unrelated to fulfilling their orders without appropriate consent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          7. Intellectual Property
        </h2>
        <p>
          Chitline and its underlying technology, trademarks, and design are owned by Chitline. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to access and use the Service during your subscription term, solely for your internal business purposes.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You retain ownership of all content you upload to the Service (menu items, photos, logos). By uploading content, you grant Chitline a non-exclusive, royalty-free licence to display, store, and process that content for the purpose of providing the Service to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">8. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is provided <strong>"as is"</strong>
          and <strong>"as available"</strong>
          without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or uninterrupted availability.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We do not guarantee that the Service will be error-free, that orders will always be delivered or transmitted successfully, or that the Service will meet your specific requirements. Internet connectivity, device failures, and third-party outages are outside our control.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          9. Limitation of Liability
        </h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Chitline and its officers, employees, and agents shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including but not limited to lost revenue, lost orders, lost data, or business interruption.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Our total cumulative liability to you for any claim arising out of or related to the Service shall not exceed the fees you paid to Chitline in the <strong>three calendar months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Nothing in these terms limits liability for death or personal injury caused by our negligence, fraud, or any liability that cannot be excluded by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">10. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          Either party may terminate the subscription at any time. Chitline may suspend or terminate your account immediately, without notice, for material breach of these Terms, non-payment, or conduct that poses a risk to the Service or other users.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Upon cancellation or termination, your access to the Service will end at the close of the current billing period (or immediately for terminations for cause). We will make your organization data available for export for
          <strong>30 days</strong>
          following termination, after which it may be permanently deleted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">11. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Province of British Columbia and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein, without regard to conflict of law principles. You agree to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts located in British Columbia for any dispute arising from these Terms or your use of the Service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          12. Dispute Resolution
        </h2>
        <p>
          In the event of a dispute, we ask that you first contact us at
          <a href="mailto:support@chitline.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">
            support@chitline.com
          </a>
          so we can attempt to resolve it informally. If the dispute cannot be resolved within 30 days of written notice, either party may pursue resolution through binding arbitration administered in British Columbia before resorting to litigation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">
          13. Changes to These Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. We will provide at least
          <strong>30 days' notice</strong>
          of material changes via email or an in-app notification. Continued use of the Service after the effective date constitutes your acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-black text-on-surface mb-3">14. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Chitline<br /> British Columbia, Canada<br />
          <a href="mailto:support@chitline.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">
            support@chitline.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-outline-variant/20 flex gap-8 text-sm font-label font-black tracking-widest uppercase text-on-surface/40">
      <a href={~p"/privacy"} class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Privacy Policy</a>
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-primary transition-colors">Home</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
